1
00:00:03,267 --> 00:00:07,433
[Subtitles by danielsangeo]

2
00:00:10,700 --> 00:00:12,667
[singing]
A horse is a horse, of course, of course

3
00:00:12,667 --> 00:00:13,933
[singing]
And no one can talk to a horse--

4
00:00:13,933 --> 00:00:15,876
Is there really no way out of here?

5
00:00:16,800 --> 00:00:18,667
How'd this even happen?

6
00:00:18,667 --> 00:00:19,467
Why?

7
00:00:20,267 --> 00:00:24,033
Yeah, it's nothing but
a Gordian knot of pipes.

8
00:00:24,033 --> 00:00:27,733
Oh, w-- No... There's nothing up there.

9
00:00:27,733 --> 00:00:32,067
Alexander the Great solved the Gordian
knot by cutting it with his sword.

10
00:00:32,067 --> 00:00:33,567
Well, I'm great.

11
00:00:33,567 --> 00:00:37,100
What's more is I would have the
brains to solve it without cheating.

12
00:00:37,100 --> 00:00:39,833
I could do better than Alexander the Great.

13
00:00:39,833 --> 00:00:42,333
Yeah, that's the only access point.

14
00:00:42,333 --> 00:00:44,200
Okay, I admit, that's a tall order,

15
00:00:44,200 --> 00:00:48,067
and I'm not the greatest position to
be making that claim at the moment,

16
00:00:48,067 --> 00:00:51,933
but c'mon, my name's Gordon, as
if I can't solve a Gordian knot.

17
00:00:53,967 --> 00:00:55,900
Yeah, there's nothing here.

18
00:00:55,900 --> 00:00:59,667
See, by cutting the knot in half, that
makes Alexander the Great look kind of dumb.

19
00:01:00,900 --> 00:01:03,013
Because then everyone
thinks he CAN'T solve it,

20
00:01:03,013 --> 00:01:05,267
he can only smash things with his sword.

21
00:01:05,267 --> 00:01:07,267
I mean, yeah, that worked--

22
00:01:07,267 --> 00:01:08,667
What equipment?

23
00:01:08,667 --> 00:01:13,633
--but if you REALLY want to deify yourself,
you solve a knot just to show you can.

24
00:01:13,633 --> 00:01:16,567
THEN you cut people's heads off--oh shit!

25
00:01:16,567 --> 00:01:17,467
AAH!

26
00:01:20,767 --> 00:01:21,300
Uh-oh...

27
00:01:22,300 --> 00:01:23,133
Oh god!

28
00:01:23,133 --> 00:01:24,167
OH GOD!

29
00:01:24,167 --> 00:01:27,167
[screaming]

30
00:01:27,167 --> 00:01:28,723
Oh god, is it gonna cave...?!

31
00:01:29,400 --> 00:01:32,167
JESUS CHRIST!

32
00:01:32,167 --> 00:01:34,667
APPARENTLY I WASN'T FUCKED ENOUGH YET!

33
00:01:34,667 --> 00:01:36,633
GLAD I COULD HIT MY QUOTA!

34
00:01:36,633 --> 00:01:37,667
IT'S FLOODING!

35
00:01:38,400 --> 00:01:39,733
[coughing]

36
00:01:39,733 --> 00:01:42,767
Smoke...there's too much smoke in here...

37
00:01:42,767 --> 00:01:45,000
Wait, it's flooding. That's what I needed.

38
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:46,500
[coughing]

39
00:01:46,500 --> 00:01:48,433
Yeah, I think I'm done here.

40
00:01:48,433 --> 00:01:49,600
I'm...

41
00:01:49,600 --> 00:01:50,700
Gah...

42
00:01:50,700 --> 00:01:52,800
I'm a problem solver.

43
00:01:52,800 --> 00:01:53,493
Yes!

44
00:02:02,467 --> 00:02:05,067
[underwater mumbling]

45
00:02:07,100 --> 00:02:08,494
[underwater mumbling]

46
00:02:14,167 --> 00:02:15,933
Oh wow. The air is better...

47
00:02:19,873 --> 00:02:21,433
The air's a lot better.

48
00:02:21,433 --> 00:02:23,933
Well if it wasn't for probably
causing an earthquake,

49
00:02:23,933 --> 00:02:26,267
I'd say that threw them off my scent.

50
00:02:26,267 --> 00:02:28,200
Well, they're not coming this way.

51
00:02:28,200 --> 00:02:31,367
Cops are like cats. They
don't like getting wet.

52
00:02:37,067 --> 00:02:39,533
Wow, I caused a lot of damage, huh?

53
00:02:39,533 --> 00:02:43,800
Yeah, fixing this is one of those
"glad it's not my job" moments.

54
00:02:43,800 --> 00:02:45,667
Assuming anyone WILL fix it.

55
00:02:45,667 --> 00:02:49,567
From what I've seen, I'm not convinced
blowing a gas line and a water main

56
00:02:49,567 --> 00:02:52,567
is enough to motivate the
city to send someone out here.

57
00:02:52,567 --> 00:02:55,833
I mean, there's bodies in the
sewer; that kind of says it all.

58
00:02:55,833 --> 00:02:58,800
Yeah, this is all going to be ruins. Again.

59
00:02:58,800 --> 00:03:01,967
This is how Rome fell apart--shit like this.

60
00:03:01,967 --> 00:03:04,067
They NEED to blame me.

61
00:03:04,067 --> 00:03:07,700
Just because I killed all those people
doesn't means I'm the source of...

62
00:03:07,700 --> 00:03:10,633
Wow, so what's the point of this?
The ladder doesn't even reach!

63
00:03:10,633 --> 00:03:12,100
And it looks welded.

64
00:03:12,100 --> 00:03:13,733
Yeah, see... Wait, what?

65
00:03:13,733 --> 00:03:15,942
Oh, you son of a bitch!

66
00:03:15,942 --> 00:03:16,833
Get...

67
00:03:16,833 --> 00:03:19,433
You have no respect for my privacy!

68
00:03:19,433 --> 00:03:20,800
Get back here!

69
00:03:20,800 --> 00:03:22,433
I said get back h...!

70
00:03:22,433 --> 00:03:24,021
You need to be taught some manners!

71
00:03:25,300 --> 00:03:28,100
Big Brother's YOUR brother, NOT MINE!

72
00:03:28,100 --> 00:03:28,900
[growls]

73
00:03:28,900 --> 00:03:33,000
Question is, can they build those faster
than I can destroy them? They might.

74
00:03:33,000 --> 00:03:35,233
At least they're clunky spy cams.

75
00:03:35,967 --> 00:03:39,367
They don't have the place wired
with fiber optics I'll never find.

76
00:03:39,367 --> 00:03:41,433
So wait. There's no path here.

77
00:03:41,433 --> 00:03:43,000
The ladder goes nowhere.

78
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:45,533
Even if that opens up, it doesn't reach.

79
00:03:45,533 --> 00:03:48,100
That means this is the official entrance.

80
00:03:48,100 --> 00:03:51,867
Some loose planks to a ledge
and no way to get--Okay, cool.

81
00:03:51,867 --> 00:03:54,667
I feel like I'm seeing
something I'm not supposed to,

82
00:03:54,667 --> 00:03:59,600
like if I keep going and lift up a grate,
I'm going to find a colony of gnomes.

83
00:03:59,600 --> 00:04:01,267
[high-pitched vocalizing]

84
00:04:01,967 --> 00:04:03,767
All right...

85
00:04:03,767 --> 00:04:08,000
Y'know, I really shouldn't rule out
the possibility of fiber-optic cameras;

86
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:09,333
there's just so much wanton ne--

87
00:04:10,300 --> 00:04:11,167
BLAH!

88
00:04:11,167 --> 00:04:13,133
C'mon, taste the Freeman!

89
00:04:13,133 --> 00:04:14,600
Oh, you wanna taste some more?!

90
00:04:14,600 --> 00:04:16,633
[screaming]

91
00:04:16,633 --> 00:04:18,300
ANOTHER CONNOISSEUR!

92
00:04:18,300 --> 00:04:19,500
HAVE A TASTE!

93
00:04:19,500 --> 00:04:20,933
HOW DO YOU LIKE IT?!

94
00:04:20,933 --> 00:04:22,000
HAVE SOME MORE!

95
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:23,600
I INSIST!

96
00:04:23,600 --> 00:04:26,100
ANOTHER SATISFIED CUSTOMER!

97
00:04:26,100 --> 00:04:27,733
ARE THERE ANY MORE?!

98
00:04:27,733 --> 00:04:29,300
I CAN DELIVER!

99
00:04:29,300 --> 00:04:32,300
C'mon, stick your head out. Just
stick your fucking head out.

100
00:04:32,300 --> 00:04:33,900
Oh, you're gonna make me wait?

101
00:04:33,900 --> 00:04:36,667
We don't have to wait! You got my attention!

102
00:04:36,667 --> 00:04:37,667
Any more...?

103
00:04:37,667 --> 00:04:40,703
Actually, they could be gone.
They may not even know I'm here.

104
00:04:40,703 --> 00:04:44,667
They could just be dropping off death bots
at every address like a paperboy route.

105
00:04:44,667 --> 00:04:46,700
Yeah, I forgot. I'm in the future.

106
00:04:46,700 --> 00:04:49,833
Maybe now, instead of the morning
paper, you just get death...

107
00:04:49,833 --> 00:04:51,477
your fucking throat slit open...

108
00:04:52,067 --> 00:04:53,767
Yeah, see? That's another one of--

109
00:04:55,903 --> 00:04:59,433
Yeah, why don't you guys go and check
that side?! There's nothing over here!

110
00:04:59,433 --> 00:05:01,233
[gunfire]
AAH!

111
00:05:01,233 --> 00:05:03,723
No, really! There's nothing here! I checked!

112
00:05:05,767 --> 00:05:06,800
See?

113
00:05:06,800 --> 00:05:09,100
Yeah, I think I would've preferred gnomes.

114
00:05:09,100 --> 00:05:11,033
I probably scared them all off.

115
00:05:11,033 --> 00:05:14,188
This must be the most action
that's been down here in centuries.

116
00:05:15,798 --> 00:05:16,547
Dah!

117
00:05:17,700 --> 00:05:20,433
I wonder if they're going to send
someone to pick up the bodies later.

118
00:05:20,433 --> 00:05:21,833
Or at least the equipment.

119
00:05:21,833 --> 00:05:24,033
They might, since they're not civilians.

120
00:05:24,033 --> 00:05:27,733
I still don't know what's going on, but
I can tell this is a crumbling empire.

121
00:05:27,733 --> 00:05:30,102
I'm getting a real Stalin-esque vibe here.

122
00:05:30,102 --> 00:05:32,267
The thing is they need me.

123
00:05:32,267 --> 00:05:35,800
Okay maybe not those two,
but the system does.

124
00:05:35,800 --> 00:05:39,167
They won the lottery with me
because nobody knows who I am.

125
00:05:39,167 --> 00:05:42,700
I'm not some political dissident
people are rallying behind.

126
00:05:42,700 --> 00:05:44,967
They can make up any story they want.

127
00:05:44,967 --> 00:05:46,033
Dammit...

128
00:05:46,033 --> 00:05:48,467
That means they can blame EVERYTHING on me

129
00:05:48,467 --> 00:05:51,300
so I'm the justification for
whatever they want to do.

130
00:05:51,300 --> 00:05:52,833
Oh, did they cut the rope?

131
00:05:52,833 --> 00:05:54,267
Yeah, looks like it.

132
00:05:54,267 --> 00:05:57,461
Maybe that's doing me a favor;
there's still helicopters outside.

133
00:05:58,533 --> 00:05:59,667
I wonder if...

134
00:06:00,600 --> 00:06:04,470
AH! THEY GOT ME! I NEED HELP! SEND BACKUP!

135
00:06:05,333 --> 00:06:06,633
...No.

136
00:06:06,633 --> 00:06:08,267
Ah, it was worth a try.

137
00:06:09,400 --> 00:06:12,267
More ammo. Sure.

138
00:06:12,267 --> 00:06:14,267
This is so bizarre.

139
00:06:14,267 --> 00:06:16,600
Actually, you know what it reminds me of?

140
00:06:16,600 --> 00:06:17,497
Yeah, exactly.

141
00:06:21,867 --> 00:06:22,867
Yeah, just keep...

142
00:06:27,533 --> 00:06:31,500
Yeah, the red robot lights,
the bodies, ammo everywhere...

143
00:06:31,500 --> 00:06:35,700
It's like the future scene in "Terminator".
They're all fighting in the tunnels?

144
00:06:35,700 --> 00:06:37,667
Well, this isn't the Terminator future.

145
00:06:37,667 --> 00:06:41,100
Seriously, I'm seeing zero AI progress.

146
00:06:41,100 --> 00:06:43,933
Ah, ammo right next to the tongue.

147
00:06:45,833 --> 00:06:49,767
Okay, stupidity check. We need to
confirm if you're still stupid.

148
00:06:50,700 --> 00:06:52,100
Whoa-ho!

149
00:06:52,100 --> 00:06:54,467
Yeah, you passed. Good job.

150
00:06:55,433 --> 00:06:58,706
All right, metal for me,
metal for you. Enjoy.

151
00:07:00,200 --> 00:07:02,267
But, yeah, I'm-- What? Oh.

152
00:07:03,867 --> 00:07:07,433
But, yeah, I'm public enemy
#1 with no stated motive.

153
00:07:07,433 --> 00:07:09,967
That's a dream come true
for the powers that be.

154
00:07:09,967 --> 00:07:11,767
And they haven't been able to kill me.

155
00:07:11,767 --> 00:07:14,933
That commune they cleared in two
minutes, but they can't get me.

156
00:07:14,933 --> 00:07:17,067
I'm the gift that keeps on giving.

157
00:07:17,067 --> 00:07:20,700
I'm a boogeyman license for them
to do whatever the hell they want.

158
00:07:20,700 --> 00:07:22,467
Too bad that doesn't help ME any.

159
00:07:22,467 --> 00:07:26,100
Ah, shit. I think I see
what's happening now.

160
00:07:26,100 --> 00:07:30,100
I'm just here to destabilize,
or maybe just as a decoy.

161
00:07:30,100 --> 00:07:34,167
The CIA's not in power anymore,
so that means I'm plan B.

162
00:07:34,167 --> 00:07:38,267
They're doing the...
Lambda? There's no formulas!

163
00:07:38,267 --> 00:07:39,567
I think that's just a tagger trying to--

164
00:07:39,567 --> 00:07:42,633
[screaming]

165
00:07:42,633 --> 00:07:44,933
But yeah, not a damned thing's changed.

166
00:07:44,933 --> 00:07:47,967
The CIA is just doing the
classic proxy war bullshit

167
00:07:47,967 --> 00:07:49,867
to try and bring down this regime.

168
00:07:49,867 --> 00:07:52,500
They're probably unofficially
arming rebels elsewhere

169
00:07:52,500 --> 00:07:55,167
because that always works in the long term.

170
00:07:55,167 --> 00:07:58,681
Meanwhile, my job is just
a fucking chaos magnet.

171
00:07:59,333 --> 00:08:02,633
Yeah, that's just graffiti.
These aren't scientists.

172
00:08:02,633 --> 00:08:05,067
So it doesn't matter to
them whether I live or die,

173
00:08:05,067 --> 00:08:07,500
just as long I'm making a big splash.

174
00:08:09,067 --> 00:08:10,967
Okay, so I get that I'm expendable,

175
00:08:10,967 --> 00:08:15,067
but even then, the way they
handled this is SO fucked.

176
00:08:15,067 --> 00:08:18,433
Wait, scratch that! No! I'm not expendable!

177
00:08:18,433 --> 00:08:21,932
Wow, this is really polluted. Shit.

178
00:08:21,932 --> 00:08:25,833
[chopper whirring]

179
00:08:25,833 --> 00:08:27,546
Okay, I don't see anything.

180
00:08:30,100 --> 00:08:32,993
But yeah, I'm not expendable
because, one, it's me,

181
00:08:34,167 --> 00:08:37,700
two, they probably think they're
being clever by telling me jack shit,

182
00:08:37,700 --> 00:08:39,900
because then I can't talk if I'm captured.

183
00:08:39,900 --> 00:08:42,778
But there's a big difference
between need-to-know only...

184
00:08:43,733 --> 00:08:45,867
...and know nothing.

185
00:08:45,867 --> 00:08:49,333
Just because I don't know what's going
on doesn't mean I don't KNOW things.

186
00:08:49,333 --> 00:08:51,433
I'm one of the few people on the PLANET--

187
00:08:52,000 --> 00:08:53,667
More bodies...

188
00:08:53,667 --> 00:08:55,867
--that could replicate Kleiner's work.

189
00:08:55,867 --> 00:09:00,133
My division could have had teleporters
and god knows what else given enough time.

190
00:09:00,133 --> 00:09:04,200
What they did would be like if we had
sent Einstein BACK to Nazi Germany

191
00:09:04,200 --> 00:09:07,466
and just dropped him off at the train
station with no papers or money.

192
00:09:08,267 --> 00:09:09,833
[gunfire]
What now?

193
00:09:09,833 --> 00:09:11,200
[gunfire]
REBEL #1: Haha! I got one!

194
00:09:13,567 --> 00:09:16,367
Freeze!
REBEL #1: Hey, you're Freeman, aren't you?

195
00:09:16,367 --> 00:09:17,500
REBEL #1: We got word you were coming.

196
00:09:17,500 --> 00:09:18,867
I'm listening...

197
00:09:18,867 --> 00:09:20,167
REBEL #1: You got here at a bad time.

198
00:09:20,167 --> 00:09:21,967
Yeah! I sure did!

199
00:09:21,967 --> 00:09:24,100
RADIO: Black Mesa East to
Station 6, do you read?

200
00:09:24,100 --> 00:09:26,833
RADIO: Dr. Freeman is on his way
downriver, lend him the airboat,

201
00:09:26,833 --> 00:09:28,333
RADIO: and give him all the help you can.

202
00:09:28,333 --> 00:09:30,633
Yeah.
RADIO: Gordon Freeman has returned!

203
00:09:30,633 --> 00:09:32,933
RADIO: It is critical he
reaches Black Mesa East.

204
00:09:32,933 --> 00:09:34,100
She's talking to you.

205
00:09:34,100 --> 00:09:35,900
REBEL #1: We've got some ammo
in those crates over there.

206
00:09:35,900 --> 00:09:37,167
You too, huh?

207
00:09:37,167 --> 00:09:39,400
REBEL #1: Help yourself to
supplies and keep moving.

208
00:09:39,400 --> 00:09:43,700
Wow, that's a lot. Yeah, we may
not have food or basic sanitation,

209
00:09:43,700 --> 00:09:46,333
but we have bullets. Let's give it a spin.

210
00:09:47,033 --> 00:09:48,900
Yeah, it has some punch, huh?

211
00:09:49,700 --> 00:09:51,733
Yeah, I'm thinking I missed part of history,

212
00:09:51,733 --> 00:09:54,567
where at some point bullets got subsidized.

213
00:09:54,567 --> 00:09:57,733
Like all that cheese they stored
in the mines back in the 80s?

214
00:09:57,733 --> 00:09:59,833
[Geiger counter clicks]
Oh, what the fuck?! That's radioactive!

215
00:09:59,833 --> 00:10:04,133
Can I turn back? No? Okay, fine,
GO go! Exposure time is the key.

216
00:10:04,133 --> 00:10:07,500
Oh good. Lots of metal to absorb
it all. That's what I want to see.

217
00:10:07,500 --> 00:10:10,700
God DAMMIT! Sending me through radioactive--

218
00:10:10,700 --> 00:10:11,300
REBEL #2: Incoming!

219
00:10:11,300 --> 00:10:12,633
What?
REBEL #3: They're shelling us!

220
00:10:13,200 --> 00:10:15,001
JESUS CHRIST!

221
00:10:16,867 --> 00:10:17,833
OH!

222
00:10:19,000 --> 00:10:19,500
Th...

223
00:10:21,833 --> 00:10:22,967
They're like popcorn.

224
00:10:23,767 --> 00:10:26,133
I can't believe we're weaponizing them!

225
00:10:26,133 --> 00:10:26,900
Ugh.

226
00:10:26,900 --> 00:10:30,247
No, wait. I CAN believe that!
That's EXACTLY what we would do!

227
00:10:30,247 --> 00:10:32,829
Christ, as if we don't
have enough problems!

228
00:10:32,829 --> 00:10:33,817
That's just the worst--

229
00:10:34,353 --> 00:10:35,083
SHIT!

230
00:10:36,333 --> 00:10:40,333
I hate it when reality is
EXACTLY as bad as the stereotype!

231
00:10:40,333 --> 00:10:44,267
Because this is exactly what the
corporate stooge wanted to do in "Aliens",

232
00:10:44,267 --> 00:10:45,433
with the facehuggers!

233
00:10:46,233 --> 00:10:48,500
OH MY GOD! THEY'RE IN THE GROUND?!

234
00:10:48,500 --> 00:10:50,667
[zombie sounds]
NO! NO!

235
00:10:50,667 --> 00:10:52,000
THIS ISN'T HAPPENING!

236
00:10:52,000 --> 00:10:53,733
THIS IS COMPLETELY UNACCEPTABLE!

237
00:10:53,733 --> 00:10:58,400
GO BACK! START OVER! AND DON'T RETURN
TO ME UNTIL YOU HAVE SOMETHING BETTER!

238
00:10:58,400 --> 00:10:59,267
BLAAAH!

239
00:11:01,100 --> 00:11:03,267
BILLY, I'M VERY DISAPPOINTED IN YOU!

240
00:11:04,800 --> 00:11:08,219
IF YOU TURNED THAT IN ON
THE EXAM, I WOULD FAIL YOU!

241
00:11:08,219 --> 00:11:11,533
Holy shit! What a great route this is!

242
00:11:11,533 --> 00:11:15,133
Yeah! They even made a little board
walkway for me! How nice is that?!

243
00:11:15,133 --> 00:11:15,933
Huh?

244
00:11:15,933 --> 00:11:18,100
JESUS CHRIST!

245
00:11:18,100 --> 00:11:22,300
WELL THIS IS SUCH A NICE PLACE TO STAY,
BUT I THINK I SHOULD BE MOVING ON!

246
00:11:23,167 --> 00:11:25,167
JUMPING GIGAWATTS!

247
00:11:25,167 --> 00:11:27,900
Okay...SWIINNNG!

248
00:11:27,900 --> 00:11:30,367
Look at that. It's arcing off the box.

249
00:11:30,367 --> 00:11:31,200
There's not even a conduc--

250
00:11:31,200 --> 00:11:32,300
[zombie roars]

251
00:11:35,167 --> 00:11:37,533
Stupid diva has to make an entrance.

252
00:11:37,533 --> 00:11:40,133
I had enough of that crap at my last job.

253
00:11:40,133 --> 00:11:42,867
Trying to upstage me, that's what happens!

254
00:11:42,867 --> 00:11:44,433
Okay, where's the path?

255
00:11:44,433 --> 00:11:46,500
Oh, I'm supposed to go in there?

256
00:11:46,500 --> 00:11:49,167
I don't fucking think so!

257
00:11:49,167 --> 00:11:51,500
I'll cook if I even get NEAR that.

258
00:11:52,200 --> 00:11:54,100
I'll just have to climb around it.

259
00:11:54,100 --> 00:11:57,733
Wait, this is all metal! This
whole wall could be charged!

260
00:11:57,733 --> 00:12:00,433
The ceiling...? Is this on purpose?

261
00:12:00,433 --> 00:12:03,600
We're turning the bug zapper on
ourselves? That's what we're doing?

262
00:12:03,600 --> 00:12:05,700
I'm gaining rads! I don't
have time for this shit!

263
00:12:07,067 --> 00:12:09,733
All right, return to sender!

264
00:12:12,133 --> 00:12:14,600
Yeah, safety first, assholes!

265
00:12:14,600 --> 00:12:18,500
Sure, this may be a radioactive
waste dump being bombed by zombies,

266
00:12:18,500 --> 00:12:20,867
but that's no reason not to have standards!

267
00:12:20,867 --> 00:12:23,100
I THINK you're off, but...

268
00:12:23,100 --> 00:12:23,727
Dyow!

269
00:12:24,300 --> 00:12:28,467
This is just a bad country, wherever
this is. I don't want to live here.

270
00:12:30,167 --> 00:12:31,967
WAAAAAAAHHHH!

271
00:12:31,967 --> 00:12:32,787
STOP THAT!

272
00:12:33,400 --> 00:12:34,900
Is it a dud?

273
00:12:34,900 --> 00:12:35,633
Of course not...!

274
00:12:37,400 --> 00:12:38,352
This is a nightmare!

275
00:12:40,322 --> 00:12:42,071
It's just a pure nightmare.

276
00:12:42,071 --> 00:12:43,600
I need a flamethrower.

277
00:12:43,600 --> 00:12:44,833
That kind of says som--

278
00:12:44,833 --> 00:12:46,166
[zombie sounds]
OH MY GOD!

279
00:12:47,700 --> 00:12:50,533
Nope, nope, I'm done! I'm done here! Bye!

280
00:12:50,533 --> 00:12:51,533
[headcrab shell]

281
00:12:51,533 --> 00:12:55,600
OH?! ANOTHER BOMBING?! THAT'S NICE!
YOU GO AHEAD AND DO THAT! I'M DONE!

282
00:12:55,600 --> 00:12:58,433
Are they behind me yet? They'll get here.

283
00:12:58,433 --> 00:13:00,300
Oh, this will be interesting.

284
00:13:00,300 --> 00:13:01,600
Come with me if you want to live!

285
00:13:01,600 --> 00:13:02,633
REBEL #4: Hey, Dr. Freeman.

286
00:13:02,633 --> 00:13:03,100
Yes.

287
00:13:03,100 --> 00:13:04,833
REBEL #4: I've been hoping you'd show up.
Oh, you have huh?

288
00:13:04,833 --> 00:13:06,367
REBEL #4: Got this airboat
all gassed up and ready to go.

289
00:13:06,367 --> 00:13:08,500
Sounds good. You're cute, let's go.

290
00:13:08,500 --> 00:13:11,033
REBEL #4: It's going to be tough dodging
Civil Protection out there in the open,

291
00:13:11,033 --> 00:13:13,000
REBEL #4: but drive hard and you'll make it.

292
00:13:13,000 --> 00:13:13,711
Is that a--

293
00:13:13,711 --> 00:13:17,400
REBEL #4: You'll find more help up at
Station 7, just a few bends up the river.

294
00:13:17,400 --> 00:13:18,933
REBEL #4: It's the old red barn.

295
00:13:18,933 --> 00:13:20,063
W-what?

296
00:13:20,063 --> 00:13:21,900
REBEL #4: Climb on in, fire her up.

297
00:13:21,900 --> 00:13:23,767
Ah, she's nervous, okay.

298
00:13:23,767 --> 00:13:26,567
Well, she should be. We're
going to get overrun in minutes.

299
00:13:26,567 --> 00:13:30,200
Oh, it only seats one. Well,
that's okay. You can sit in my lap.

300
00:13:30,200 --> 00:13:32,033
REBEL #4: Go ahead and get
in the boat, Dr. Freeman.

301
00:13:32,033 --> 00:13:32,633
Yeah, but--

302
00:13:32,633 --> 00:13:33,500
REBEL #4: Get in the airboat, sir.

303
00:13:33,500 --> 00:13:35,800
Oh, "sir". She's probably military.

304
00:13:35,800 --> 00:13:37,233
REBEL #4: Climb on in, fire her up.

305
00:13:37,233 --> 00:13:38,967
Yeah, this isn't going to work.

306
00:13:38,967 --> 00:13:40,748
Okay, let's fire this up.

307
00:13:42,100 --> 00:13:43,133
Uh...

308
00:13:43,133 --> 00:13:45,833
Hey, those aliens are going to
kill you. Wanted to say that.

309
00:13:45,833 --> 00:13:46,967
REBEL #4: You'd better get going. Now.

310
00:13:46,967 --> 00:13:49,567
Oh, I'm going. Don't worry about that.

311
00:13:49,567 --> 00:13:50,394
Is this throttle?

312
00:13:51,400 --> 00:13:52,415
Oh, whoa-WHOA!

313
00:13:53,967 --> 00:13:56,167
Oh, now I'm going backw--Smooth!

314
00:13:56,167 --> 00:13:59,430
I don't know what I'm doing. I've
never driven a swamp boat before.

315
00:13:59,430 --> 00:14:03,367
Well, I'll say this. NOTHING
has changed with the ladies.

316
00:14:03,367 --> 00:14:06,267
She said she was hoping I would show up,

317
00:14:06,267 --> 00:14:10,833
so I show up. Thirty seconds later, she's
practically shoving me out the door.

318
00:14:10,833 --> 00:14:13,667
Aliens have taken over THE WORLD,

319
00:14:13,667 --> 00:14:16,376
and yet her standards are
still too high for me, huh?

320
00:14:16,376 --> 00:14:17,911
I mean, what the fuck?

321
00:14:17,911 --> 00:14:19,867
I mean, she was so not-down with me

322
00:14:19,867 --> 00:14:23,873
that she's not even going to pretend to
be nice and come with me to save her life.

323
00:14:23,873 --> 00:14:27,433
This is the test of that "If you
were the last man on Earth" question,

324
00:14:27,433 --> 00:14:29,100
would you--
[gagging]

325
00:14:29,100 --> 00:14:31,477
Jesus, this air's bad!

326
00:14:31,477 --> 00:14:33,333
And my Geiger counter's still going--

327
00:14:33,333 --> 00:14:35,191
[coughing, gagging]

328
00:14:35,191 --> 00:14:40,933
I've gotta get out here! This is a
cesspool! This is a literal cesspool!

329
00:14:40,933 --> 00:14:44,371
A radioactive cesspool with
zombies swimming in it.

330
00:14:44,371 --> 00:14:47,555
So yeah, it's the worst thing
imaginable. I've seen it.

331
00:14:47,555 --> 00:14:49,333
Wait, where the hell do I go?

332
00:14:49,333 --> 00:14:51,967
There's no passage here. Did I miss a turn?

333
00:14:51,967 --> 00:14:54,467
There's nothing to turn TO. What...?

334
00:14:54,467 --> 00:14:58,333
Okay, so she lied. There is no
river. It's just a pond of leachate.

335
00:14:58,333 --> 00:15:01,567
Actually, it's not even a pond.
This is more like a giant puddle.

336
00:15:01,567 --> 00:15:03,367
Should I go back and yell at her?

337
00:15:03,367 --> 00:15:06,618
No, she won't get it. She's
just following orders.

338
00:15:06,618 --> 00:15:07,800
"Sir"...

339
00:15:07,800 --> 00:15:10,833
She's probably dead by now anyway. I tried!

340
00:15:10,833 --> 00:15:14,867
Jeez, that's big! Friggin' Tower of Orthanc.

341
00:15:14,867 --> 00:15:16,996
Well, nice view...

342
00:15:19,833 --> 00:15:21,400
Hm, now that I think about it,

343
00:15:21,400 --> 00:15:26,200
women who try to get themselves killed
turn me off anyway. Bad investment.

